-- title:
--   Pullback of a cyclic extension step
-- statement:
--   Let $G,H$ be groups, let $f:H\to G$ be a homomorphism, let $A\trianglelefteq G$, and let $B\le G$. Suppose $B=\langle A,g\rangle$ for some $g\in G$, where brackets denote the subgroup generated by the indicated elements and subgroup. Then
--
--   $$\exists h\in H,\qquad f^{-1}(B)=\langle f^{-1}(A),h\rangle.$$
--
--   Thus a cyclic step above a normal subgroup remains cyclic after taking its inverse image. This supports the inheritance of supersolvable series.
-- source:
--   Michael C. Burkhart, Local conjugacy in prosolvable groups, https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.37678; supporting formalization lemma, LocalConjugacy/SupersolvableStructure.lean, lines 11–43; source SHA-256 c06f9eac035d521faa11c587697ded75f3b001382a70b83938592f249f234b48.

